// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Keppel_H_UrgentTask1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Clue1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P978922340" "Lady Gallant and Scarlet Squire"
// DetailString :
"P2443794733" "Two hot chixxors who wield swords and fight for truth, justice, and chivalry. Apparently Scarlet Squire can't find Lady Gallant."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Clue2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2275460643" "Clockwork"
// DetailString :
"P4280575659" "These Clockwork are WAY more advanced than those on Primal Earth. Luckily they aren't too smart. Anti-Matter must have watched Terminator and thought better than to make them too smart."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Clue3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1163489766" "Jamming Device"
// DetailString :
"P1266738274" "Apparently Anti-Matter has an orbital cannon pointed at the enclosure. The slightest hint of trouble reaches his ears and he pushes a button and the place turns into a radioactive smear on the face of the planet. Jamming the communications grid will prevent that signal from getting sent to Anti-Matter."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P561900101" "So, I guess I have some explaning to do, but unfortunately, time is of critical scarcity at this juncture, your explanation will have to wait!<br><br>The first order of business is a matter of healing a rift... no, not the dimensional rift... ha ha, that is a good one though!<br><br>But I drift. I'm afraid that a primal heroine is rather put off at me for pulling her through the rift, as if my hands pulled a lever to do so.<br><br>Anyway, so far she has seemed gracious enough to dismantle any clockworks that wander too close to our position, but, I want to ensure that she knows how grateful we are for her doing so. Since my attempts to speak to her have, well, failed, I thought maybe you would have better luck.<br><br>Her name is Scarlet Squire."
// AcceptString :
"P2831985678" "Talk to Scarlet Squire"
// SendOffString :
"P2631260484" "Please see if you can help Ms. Scarlet. I fear that her distaste for us and the hand we played in creating the rift that trapped her might soon shift her attitude to a more hostile stance than it is already."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Keppel_H_UrgentTask1_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4181382566" "Have you spoken with Scarlet Squire yet? She seems upset, but whenever I try to talk to her she just glares at me and tells me that I've done enough already."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2830292347" "Dr. Keppel is a lunatic! He's the one who brought us here in the first place, isn't he? Now he's trying to get us to help him!? The nerve!<br><br>I'm sorry, I'm normally all for helping people, but... I think you might be in a better frame of mind to help him. I need to focus on finding my mentor, Lady Gallant."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Keppel_H_UrgentTask1_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P4159088995" "Return to Dr. Keppel"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1481046330" "See if you can help Dr. Keppel, I have to focus on finding Lady Gallant."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1471268909" "I'm sorry to hear that Ms. Scarlet won't help. I feel for her, I really do, but right now we haven't got time to settle our differences about how you all got here. That can wait until after we aren't in danger of being remotely atomized!<br><br> At any rate, now I need you to fight some clockwork around here to put you higher than us on their threat list. It is nothing personal, it's just that you can handle them while we cannot. You understand."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Keppel_H_UrgentTask1_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2047281503" "Defeat Clockwork"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1183575192" "Have you engaged the clockwork as I asked?<br><br>Anti-Matter's clockwork are far more advanced than the crude automotons from your world. Even still, they have their quirks which can be taken advantage of, such as their rudimentry threat priority system.<br><br>They aren't designed to handle such a number of threats, this is due to them being built with a X73-A52 datacore...<br><br>Oh, I do suppose I am rambling, sorry."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P572714409" "Threat detected. Priority list updated. Terminate immediately."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1570731323" "Good job on destroying those clockwork, they may be advanced technology, but they are fairly single minded when it comes to eliminating what they deem to be hostile targets.<br><br>Speaking of targets, we are one. The clockwork will soon determine that they cannot contain the situation here and send a signal to Anti-Matter's orbital lab to destroy the enclosure. <br><br>You, however, are going to help me jam that signal... or we'll all die in a concentrated anti-proton volley fired from orbit. Simple choice, really.<br><br>Simply go to each of the five communication emitters and punch in these numbers. Once all five have been correctly sequenced all communication out of the enclosure will be jammed and replaced with false chatter to avoid suspicions."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Keppel_H_UrgentTask1_Part4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3834538168" "Activate the Jamming Devices"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P860220167" "Quickly now, you must activate all five of the jamming devices around the compound before the Clockwork send a signal to Anti-Matter's orbital lab and he destroys us from orbit.<br><br>I am so not joking."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4006950893" "Great job on activating the jammers. According to my readings they are working flawlessly, and on the first try as well!<br><br>Testing is so over rated."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2345280457" "Now that we've isolated our little problem out here and don't have to worry about imminent annihilation, we can focus on the sources of our problems rather than the symptoms.<br><br>I have plenty for you to do around here, but I know that Ms. Scarlet needs your help as well, even if she is too proud to admit it.<br><br>Thanks again, {HeroName}, we all owe you our lives, even if we are partially responsible for dragging you all into this mess... which wouldn't have happened if we hadn't opened the rift in the first place... ahem, no use over thinking it, as I always say."
// RandomFameString :
"P856364347" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Keppel_H_Task1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DrKeppelReport1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2993473222" "Dr. Keppel's Report"
// DetailString :
"P3110681231" "<3<3<3"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DevouredRootsSamples 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1553294755" "Devoured Roots Samples"
// DetailString :
"P1472040669" "You've managed to strip several pieces off of the devoured roots around the enclosure and place them in these test tubes. They thrash wildly against the glass, and for a moment you worry that they might break free.<br><br>You need to deliver these to Dr. Leta."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DrLetaReport1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3658525400" "Dr. Leta's Report"
// DetailString :
"P950671963" "FU FU FU"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1926414717" "The devouring earth seeded the ground with seeds before we even set about construction of this site. Now those seeds have started growing into writhing roots, possibly at the behest of their brethren outside of the enclosure shield. I need you to destroy some of those roots and gather some samples.<br><br>Oh, here, put them in these test tubes. I'm sure they'll be perfectly safe."
// AcceptString :
"P1831329443" "Destroy devouring roots"
// SendOffString :
"P3668772381" "Once you've gathered the samples take them and this report over to Dr. Leta in Facility B. It's on the other side of the enclosure, so you'll likely have to fend off some clockwork on your way.<br><br>Dr. Leta will have a report for you to bring to me. I wish our network was working, it would make this all so much easier."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Keppel_H_Task1_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2108989672" "Destroy Devouring Roots"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2233506862" "Have you gathered the appropriate samples of the Devouring Roots as I asked? You'll need to take them over to Dr. Leta with that report I gave you. We must understand the threat they pose, if any, to the enclosure."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P137125250" "Subject detected.<em t=1>Infection probability 78.2%.<em t=2>Terminate."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3080161542" "You got the devouring roots samples."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Keppel_H_Task1_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1913594934" "Deliver samples and report to Dr. Leta"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P53752155" "Now that you have the Devouring Root samples I need you to deliver them to Dr. Leta. Don't forget to give her my report as well."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1500899371" "What do you want?<br><br>Devoured roots samples? Wow, let me guess, this was one of Keppel's brilliant ideas.<br><br>Well, I'd better take those off your hands before you get us all infected... What's that? Let me see that report.<br><br>Hmph! Waste of my time. Here, take this report to Keppel and tell him to try and send more detailed reports in the future, his vaguarities and assumptions are driving me nuts."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P886634600" "Thank you, {HeroName}. I'll read over Dr. Leta's report in a minute. I swear, I'll never understand that woman. She's cold one minute, and perfectly amiable the next.<br><br>Maybe it's me. It would certainly explain a lot of my past failures and almost all of the misunderstandings between me and those studen...<br><br>Oh, you're still here. Good! I have another task for you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL2-9_RE_Keppel_H_Task2a 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1022929430" "We've got a problem. No, scratch that. We have an imminent disaster.<br><br>More primals have escaped from another prison block and, according to the clockwork chatter I've tapped into, they intend to destroy one of the enclosure's power generators. I need you to go stop them before they get us all killed."
// AcceptString :
"P983964404" "Protect the Generator"
// SendOffString :
"P3281466841" "Good. If they destroy that generator then the jammers you helped set up might lose power. It's also fairly likely that the shield around the enclosure will fail. This is all due to a poor engineering choice in routing all the power through the K-7 access tubes to the...<br><br>You know what, you're right, that isn't important. Just go stop them before it's too late."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3286034628" "Umm. Aren't you supposed to be stopping a bunch of primals from destroying that power generator?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1168422566" "Ho boy... It's just you against a prison full of primal villains. Time to shine."

